{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 evidence (guard proven RED before the fix), recorded per the AC.\n\nRemoving the `sys.path` insert from `scripts/canary_bridge.py` and running the new guard:\n\n    scripts/canary_bridge.py:27: import alert_dedup (sys.path.insert above: False; derives from __file__: False)\n    AssertionError: a standalone bare `pytest` run of test_reconcile_bridge_canary_class.py failed:\n    1 failed, 1 passed  ->  after restoring the insert: 2 passed\n\nBoth guard tests go RED against the defect and GREEN with the fix.\n\nNote on the dynamic guard: the first draft used `--collect-only`, which stayed GREEN against the live defect — the failure surfaces at module-scoped fixture setup (where canary_bridge.py is loaded by path), which collection never reaches. The test now RUNS the module instead. Worth recording because it is the same change-detector trap this ticket is about.\n\nGates: lint + format + typecheck clean; full `tests/unit tests/scripts` = 10069 passed, 38 skipped, exit 0. Gerrit change 1606."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786501479637742001,"uuid":"19dc528a-2d6b-42bd-8d7d-db6ae23af6ed"}